 	if (miatoll) {
 		/*
-		 * DT (fragment@35): vdd pm6150_l10 1.8 V, avdd pm6150l_l7 3.0 V,
-		 * no power GPIO; reset gpio8 active-low 20 ms then 200 ms boot
-		 * wait; irq gpio9 level-low; bus pins gpio6/7 (function "gpio"
-		 * = TLMM mux 0, pull-up, 2 mA — the DT sleep state).
-		 * 0096: pm6150 sits at SID0 (DT pm6150@0), so ppid for ldoa10
-		 * is 0x01d — earlier observer probes hardcoded SID4 and never
-		 * tried it. Dump the PM6150 ON reference (l11, enabled 1.8 V
-		 * under Android), the target ldoa10, and the PM6150L
-		 * references (ldoc3 ON / ldoc2 OFF); then fire Linux order
-		 * SLEEP -> WAKE -> ACTIVE on ldoa10 with a dump between each
-		 * state. rh_fire prints RPMh response words, so a rejected
-		 * vote is visible. ldoc7 remains a bus-only test.
+		 * 0097: 0096 read the real rail (ldoa10, SID0/0x1d) directly —
+		 * SLEEP vote flips reg00 00->01 (the ON pattern), WAKE flips it
+		 * back and touches reg45, ACTIVE restores pre; the Linux-order
+		 * triple therefore ends exactly where XBL left the rail (off)
+		 * and the clamp never released. Fire SLEEP ONLY so the rail
+		 * ends in the sleep-vote state, then test the bus.
 		 */
 		st.bb = true;
 		st.bb_sda = 6;
